<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_BPWithID" Id="{e3bfa99b-9d0a-4973-9793-594c4c68e1ba}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_BPWithID : copy a beam-parameter set into an arbiter-internal set and
    stamp it with the arbiter request ID.

    Purpose:
        Turn a caller's ST_BeamParams request into the ST_BP_ArbInternal image
        that FB_Arbiter stores in its assertion pool: the beam parameters are
        copied (SIZEOF(BP)) into the ST_BeamParams part at the start of the
        result, and the request identifier is written into
        ST_BP_ArbInternal.nId, so a stored assertion can be traced back to the
        device and state that requested it.

    Usage:
        Assign the result wherever an ST_BP_ArbInternal is needed, i.e. when
        packing a beam-parameter request together with the ID it was
        registered under. BP must reference an ST_BeamParams owned by the
        caller - the referenced set is only read, never modified - and must
        be a valid reference, because the POU does not check it. ID must be
        the identifier the caller registers the request under, since that
        becomes the assertion-pool key. This helper does NOT set the remaining
        arbiter-internal bookkeeping fields: LiveInTable and sDevName are left
        as the function result already holds them, so a caller that puts the
        result into the pool must set both itself (as FB_Arbiter.AddRequest
        does with BP_Int.LiveInTable := TRUE and BP_Int.sDevName := sDevName).

    Objectives:
        - One place that performs the 'pack the ID into the beam-parameter
          set' step, instead of each consumer open-coding the MEMCPY plus the
          nId assignment.
        - Keep the copied beam parameters byte-identical to the source set, so
          the arbiter evaluates exactly the values that were requested.
        - State the identifier contract: ID is the caller-owned request /app/namespaces/d6f73763-31bc-4bea-8f49-b5906058e129/
          assertion ID (unique per device + state combination), not an arbiter,
          EPICS or enum ID. 0 and PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID are reserved
          'not found' values (see F_ValidReqID); this helper does not validate
          them, so the caller must.

    History:
        2020-08-07  Alex Wallace : Created - first attempt at packing the ID
                                   into the arbiter pool so we can figure out
                                   where requests come from.
        2026-11-27  Audit fix    : Header and declaration comments added; no
                                   code change (audit finding #254).
*)
FUNCTION F_BPWithID : ST_BP_ArbInternal
VAR_INPUT
    // Beam-parameter set to copy. Must reference a valid ST_BeamParams owned
    // by the caller; it is read only. Units: as declared in ST_BeamParams
    // (nTran % pre-optic, nRate Hz, neVRange/nBCRange bitmasks, apertures mm).
    BP : REFERENCE TO ST_BeamParams;
    // Arbiter request (assertion) identifier stamped into the result's
    // ST_BP_ArbInternal.nId. It is the caller's own request/state ID, unique
    // per device + state combination, and FB_Arbiter uses it as the
    // assertion-pool key. Reserved / invalid values: 0 and
    // PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID (16#FFFFFFFF) - not validated here, see
    // F_ValidReqID. Units: none (identifier).
    ID : DWORD;
END_VAR
VAR
    // Declared but unused: the implementation copies straight into the
    // function result F_BPWithID, so nothing is ever staged through this
    // local. Retained as declared scratch space - no behaviour depends on it.
    BpInt : ST_BP_ArbInternal;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[MEMCPY(ADR(F_BPWithID), ADR(BP), SIZEOF(BP));
F_BPWithID.nId := ID;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>